Spec: Tests

Purpose:
  Automated `pytest` tests for the `aikana` package, run without a network or a running server.

Structure:
  ./conftest.py: shared fixtures wiring an in-process client and every feature's services on a temporary database
  ./test_auth.py: in-process client tests of the admin login and logout, the shell's login/logout link and the
    password's secrecy
  ./test_courses.py: in-process client tests of the courses page, its create form and its edit and delete dialogs
  ./test_dates.py: unit tests for the shared Europe/Helsinki date policy
  ./test_day_dialog.py: in-process client tests of the admin day dialog's forms, its guard and its grid and
    weekly-table swaps
  ./test_main.py: in-process client tests of the app entry point, the semester routes and the wall planner's
    rendering
  ./test_no_teach_weeks.py: unit tests for the NoTeachWeek package's pure domain rules
  ./test_realizations.py: in-process client tests of the courses page's add, edit and delete realization dialogs and
    of the weekly view's states, fallbacks, week sub-rows and Share button
  ./test_semester_domain.py: unit tests for the Semester package's pure domain rules
  ./test_services.py: service-layer validation tests against temporary databases
  ./test_shared.py: tests of the shared kernel's database factory and page shell

Owns:
  ./test_*.py
  ./conftest.py

Depends on:
  /src/aikana/aikana.sdd

Must:
  Tests exercise the app through an in-process client and leave no files behind in the repository.
  Tests never touch `/data`: they build each app or service on a temporary database through @create_app and
  @create_database, which is possible because importing `aikana.main` has no side effects.
